      "id": "2026-11-18-use-floating-rect-popups-whose-text-scrolls-410fc4f1",
      "kind": "behavior",
      "summary": "Take the whole `RangeGeometry`, hide the popup once no line of its text is in the editor's visible area, and return `shown`, which says whether the popup is drawn. Pass `hideWhenClipped: false` to keep a popup shown, such as a form someone is typing in.",
      "details": [],
      "migrationNotes": [
        "Pass the whole geometry from `useSelectionGeometry` in place of `geometry.boundingRect`.",
        "Read `shown` in place of `isPositioned`, and spread `style` in place of `floatingStyles`."
      ],
